rce seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadmea">Cadmea</a> by a coup de main; it was expelled three years later and a democratic constitution set up</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">371 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Theban forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> defeated the Spartans at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Battle of Leuctra</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">362 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> died at the Battle of Mantinea and Thebes sank back to a secondary power</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">338 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> defeated Thebes and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> at the Battle of Chaeronea</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">335 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> destroyed Thebes after its revolt and sold its people into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">315 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassander">Cassander</a> re-established Thebes with labour and money from other Greek cities</span></li></ol>
